<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Boksin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 663</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a> · Also known as Gwisil Boksin</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Boksin was a Baekje general and member of the royal family who led the movement to restore Baekje after its conquest by Tang and Silla in 660. With the monk Dochim he held out at Juryu fortress, brought Prince <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buyeo-pung">Buyeo Pung</a> back from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> and won Yamato support. He killed Dochim in a quarrel and was in turn killed by Buyeo Pung in 663, shortly before the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-baekgang">Battle of Baekgang</a>.</p></div>
